----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is an unofficial fork of openMSX
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

It adds emulation of the Y8960 Cartridge, a sound cartridge for the MSX
designed by HRA! (hra1129). The hardware itself is still work in progress,
so the emulation follows a moving target and is expected to change.

Upstream openMSX does not contain any of this. Report problems to this fork,
not to the openMSX developers.

    this fork: https://github.com/madscient/openMSX_Y8960
    upstream:  https://github.com/openMSX/openMSX

What is added
-------------

The cartridge is the extension HRA_Y8960 (share/extensions/HRA_Y8960.xml):

    openmsx -machine <machine> -ext HRA_Y8960

It is built from these devices:

    Y8960-OPLL       2x YM2413 with a per-channel preset tone bank
    Y8960-OPL2       2x YM3812 with waveform select, each with an ADPCM-B
    Y8960-ADPCM-RAM  the 256KB ADPCM sample memory the two OPL2 share
    Y8960-SSGS       two YM2149-compatible SSGs with 4-bit panpots
    Y8960-DCSG       2x SN76489-compatible DCSG
    MSX-TIMER        the cartridge's timer
    Y8960-MIXER      the cartridge's digital mixer and output switch
    Y8960 ROM type   SCC, the cartridge's mapper, its I/O enablers and the
                     memory-mapped access to the sound chips

The cartridge does not feed its sound back into the MSX, so by default only
the Y8960's own output is heard. The setting y8960-mixer_output selects
y8960, msx or mix.

Known limitations:

    - The mixer registers (B6h-B7h) keep the values written to them but do
      not change the gains yet: their layout is not specified.
    - The mapper keeps ROM (banks 0-15) and 128KB of RAM (banks 16-31) as
      separate spaces, whereas the FPGA design has one 256KB space. This
      waits for the hardware specification to settle.
    - There is no real hardware to compare with. The behaviour follows the
      specification and the FPGA sources as they were read.

Notes for this fork are under doc/fork/ in the repository. They are written
in Japanese and are aimed at developers, not at end users.

Credits
-------

The Y8960 emulation started from the work of buppu3, taken from the 'y8960'
branch of https://github.com/buppu3/openMSX and rebased onto current
openMSX. Their commits keep their original authorship. The V9968 VDP
emulation that lives on the same branch is deliberately not included here.

The hardware, its documentation and the FPGA sources are by HRA! (hra1129),
https://github.com/hra1129/Y8960_Cartridge . Nothing from that repository is
copied into this one: its license forbids commercial use, which is not
compatible with the GPL that openMSX is released under. The emulation was
written from reading the specification.

src/sound/YM2413NukeYKTBanked.cc carries preset tone data for the OPLL-X,
OPLL-P and VRC7 tone banks in addition to the YM2413 ones. That data comes
from "Copyright free OPLL(x) ROM patches" by David Viens and Hubert
Lamontagne:

    https://github.com/plgDavid/misc/wiki/Copyright-free-OPLL(x)-ROM-patches

    Copyright free OPLL(x) ROM patches
    (C) David Viens, Hubert Lamontagne
    Licensed under CC BY-SA.

Redistribution has to keep that attribution.

